comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T18:28:09.956Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: the public SDK now exposes a versioned corpus-shape schema and five deterministic built-ins (scratch, representative, deep-graph, multi-decade, disconnected-archive). The generator materializes authors, schema customizations, annotations, typed edges, history depth, time span, parents and disconnected archives, emits measured shape manifests, and fails closed on declaration drift. A committed same-count scratch-versus-representative report compares claim/context/create/get/list/next/search p95 with a declared 20 percent materiality margin."
  "2026-07-29T18:36:32.148Z","harness:codex","Linked benchmark hygiene: the executable comparison link writes to an explicit temporary output so repeated PM verification cannot rewrite the committed evidence report; the committed report remains a deliberate versioned artifact generated for this delivery."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T18:28:11.006Z","harness:codex","Compatibility decision: scale budgets are keyed by shape, with a scratch fallback to legacy unqualified budget records so existing benchmark consumers do not break while new population-specific evidence remains attributable."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T18:28:12.101Z","harness:codex","Item count alone is not a corpus contract. Reproducible performance evidence needs a versioned population declaration, measured conformance after generation, and shape-qualified thresholds; otherwise constants fitted to one shallow synthetic population look universal."
